    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so basically you're saying the \"neighborhood character\" argument is just a way to avoid the actual solution. if it's basically a proven fact that more density equals better affordability and less environmental impact, why even bother giving the other side much weight? why is it even a debate if the density path is clearly the better one for the future?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
